{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,1]],"date-time":"2026-06-01T13:49:32Z","timestamp":1780321772927,"version":"3.54.1"},"reference-count":55,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"11","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2007,6,27]],"date-time":"2007-06-27T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1182902400000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Glia"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2007,8,15]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title><jats:p>The Schwann cell basal lamina acts as an organizer of peripheral nerve tissue and influences many aspects of cell behavior during development and regeneration. A principal component of the Schwann cell basal lamina is laminin\u20102. This study was undertaken to identify Schwann cell receptors for laminin\u20102. We found that among several Schwann cell integrins that can potentially interact with laminin\u20102, only \u03b17\u03b21 bound to laminin\u20102\u2010Sepharose. Dystroglycan, a non\u2010integrin Schwann cell receptor for laminin\u20102 identified previously, was also found to bind to laminin\u20102\u2010Sepharose. Antibody to the \u03b17 integrin subunit partially inhibited Schwann cell adhesion to laminin\u20102. Small interfering RNA\u2010mediated suppression of either \u03b17 integrin or dystroglycan expression decreased adhesion and spreading of Schwann cells on laminin\u20102, whereas knocking down both proteins together inhibited adhesion and spreading on laminin\u20102 almost completely. \u03b17 integrin and dystroglycan both colocalized with laminin\u20102 containing basal lamina tubes in differentiating neuron\u2013Schwann cell cocultures. The \u03b17\u03b21 integrin also coprecipitates with focal adhesion kinase in differentiating cocultures. These findings strongly suggest that \u03b17\u03b21 integrin is a Schwann cell receptor for laminin\u20102 that provides transmembrane linkage between the Schwann cell basal lamina and cytoskeleton. \u00a9 2007 Wiley\u2010Liss, Inc.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/glia.20536","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2007,6,27]],"date-time":"2007-06-27T21:47:23Z","timestamp":1182980843000},"page":"1134-1144","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":22,"title":["\u03b17\u03b21 integrin is a receptor for laminin\u20102 on Schwann cells"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"55","author":[{"given":"Michael A.","family":"Chernousov","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Stephen J.","family":"Kaufman","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Richard C.","family":"Stahl","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Katrina","family":"Rothblum","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"David J.","family":"Carey","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2007,6,27]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_6_2_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1242\/jcs.01234"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0022-510X(73)90009-9"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_4_1","first-page":"299","volume-title":"Peripheral neuropathy","author":"Bunge MB","year":"1993"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_5_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1083\/jcb.152.6.1207"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_6_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1083\/jcb.111.5.2053"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_7_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0165-3806(87)90142-8"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_8_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1083\/jcb.102.6.2254"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_9_1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"3776","DOI":"10.1523\/JNEUROSCI.20-10-